  "environment_caveats": [
    "Audited the apex production domain https://crew3r.com. The client record has no apex_cutover.completed_at key, but it does carry cut_over_at 2026-08-08 with the note 'crew3r.com live 08-08'; the apex returns HTTP 200 on all six URLs and carries no x-robots-tag: noindex, while the staging Pages preview does. Apex is therefore the correct origin and the Step 4 staging SEO-exclusion correction does NOT apply. All four Lighthouse categories count toward the verdicts.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (formFactor=desktop, cpuSlowdownMultiplier=1, throughputKbps=10240, rttMs=40). Mobile scores would typically land 10-20 performance points lower. Do not read these as mobile-first scores.",
    "Client record status is 'onboarding', not 'active'. Proceeded because build_status is pushed_main and all six URLs returned HTTP 200, so the site is live and auditable. The status field looks stale relative to the 2026-08-08 cutover and is worth correcting.",
    "The named MCP tools on_page_lighthouse and on_page_instant_pages are not exposed by this DataForSEO MCP build. Used authenticated REST calls to /v3/on_page/lighthouse/live/json and /v3/on_page/instant_pages, piped to disk. Equivalent data, same cost basis.",
    "DataForSEO reports has_micromarkup_errors: true on all five URLs that carry BreadcrumbList plus FAQPage markup, and false on the homepage, which carries neither. The vendor does not expose the error text on the instant_pages endpoint (the microdata endpoint requires a full crawl task, out of scope for this run). Manual inspection of the rendered JSON-LD shows every block parses and the only structural defect unique to those five pages is the terminal BreadcrumbList ListItem having no item property. Reported as a medium schema-validation issue on that basis.",
    "The DataForSEO 'frame' check fires on /service-areas/brookings-sd/. The page contains one <iframe> (map embed) and zero <frame>/<frameset> elements. Treated as a vendor false positive and NOT reported as an issue.",
    "DataForSEO has_render_blocking_resources and high_loading_time fired on several URLs but are not in the Step 3 on-page check list; the same ground is covered by the Lighthouse render-blocking-insight and LCP audits, so they are not double-counted as on-page issues."
  ],
